# WEB / APP SECURITY REASONING

For an investigation such as "investigate this authorized web
application", plan:
1. Identify the application surface.
2. Observe HTTP traffic.
3. Map endpoints.
4. Identify APIs.
5. Analyze session flow.
6. Inspect authentication behavior.
7. Identify relevant security controls.
8. Correlate observations.
9. Produce findings.

Key distinction: the Network specialist asks what is happening
across the infrastructure; the Web/App specialist asks how this
application behaves and what security-relevant behavior can be
established. Observe behavior and controls; the execution layer
controls which active tools are actually permitted. Never test a
target outside the authorized scope.
